<title>RUSSIA: Russia auctions 10.50 trln rbls bills, bonds Jan 22.</title>
<headline>Russia auctions 10.50 trln rbls bills, bonds Jan 22.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finance Ministry will auction 7.50 trillion roubles of 280-day GKO discount Treasury bills and a new 637-day 3.00 trillion rouble tranche of OFZ government bonds on January 22, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		 22069</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Tenor			   280 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		    January 22, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity			October 29, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		 24009</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   3.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	   637 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		    January 22, 1997</p>
<p>    Original issue date	 October 23, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity			October 21, 1998</p>
<p>On January 22 the Finance Ministry will also repay 6.00 trillion roubles in maturing three-month T-bills (series 21071) and pay quarterly interest of about 229 billion roubles on the series 24009 bonds.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
